OL,3,GNEWSAChildren's centre chief objects
OL,4,Aover plan for homelessness centre next
OL,5,Adoor
OL,6,
OL,7,FA children's centre has said it is
OL,8,F"under threat" because of plans for a
OL,9,Fhomelessness service to move into a
OL,10,Fbuilding next door.
OL,12,FFoodstock, which aims to tackle poverty
OL,13,Fin Belfast, runs the children's centre
OL,14,Fand its founder, independent councillor
OL,15,FPaul Doherty, said the move is a "child
OL,16,Fsafeguarding issue".
OL,18,FHe said the concern is "not who is
OL,19,Fturning up, but there may be people
OL,20,Fturning up and attending in distress,
OL,21,Fcrisis or in unpredictable
OL,22,Fcircumstances".
OL,23,APub: 18-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
